I committed this as 10276d24 and the full suite passes, but it doesn't do what the task title says. /map still ignores the /cd deny list, and nothing changes for users today. The register still went from 5 to 4.

Why the title was wrong. commands_map.rs has one production check_path call, in build_repo_map_core. Only the repo map built into the system prompt at startup (cli.rs → generate_repo_map_for_prompt) passes it a fence. The /map command passes none, on purpose since #1002: it prints to you, not to the provider, so --deny-dir doesn't apply to it either. Making /map obey the /cd list alone would have made /cd stricter than the launch flag. So I wired the real check and rewrote the commit title to say what it does.

The directory check from the plan. The map reads git ls-files / rev-parse from the current working directory, which /cd changes, so it would read the right directory. But the one fenced reader runs only once at startup, before any /cd. The /cd list is always empty when it runs. What the wiring buys is that if the prompt map is ever rebuilt after a /cd, denied files stay out instead of leaking in.

What changed:
• **src/commands_map.rs:**
  • The startup-fence check runs first, unchanged. Then the /cd list is checked via cd_denied_dir_refusal_with.
  • Omitted files are now counted separately for each list (a small MapOmitted { fence, cd } struct).
  • A new count-only stderr note, repo_map_cd_deny_note, ends with CD_DENY_SOURCE_NOTE. That way a /cd omission is never blamed on --deny-dir.
• **`src/cd_config_note.rs:** removed the commands_map.rs row from UNWIRED_CHECK_PATH_READERS` (5 → 4).
• **`ARCHITECTURE.md:** updated only the residue list in the /cd` deny entry. It now says the change is invisible to users today.

Tests, all with a temp directory and an injected /cd list rather than the global:
• A /cd entry for private/ drops it from the map. The sibling file still renders identically (assert_eq).
• An empty /cd list, or one naming an unrelated folder, gives byte-identical output, with and without a startup fence.
• If both lists name the same folder, the omission counts against the startup fence.
• The new note is silent at zero and has no glyphs in plain mode.

Positive control (one change at a time, restored in the same command): disabling the new /cd check failed exactly two tests by name: cd_deny_entry_omits_its_subdirectory_and_keeps_the_sibling and the repo-wide guard no_check_path_reader_skips_the_cd_deny_list_unregistered. The byte-identical tests stayed green. After restoring, all four checks pass: 6511 tests, 0 failed; clippy with -D warnings, fmt and build are clean.

I posted a comment on #869 with the new count, the four files left (commands_project.rs, commands_rename.rs, context.rs, skill_fence.rs) and the corrected scope. The commit isn't pushed yet; the session wrap-up pushes it.
